---
title: "severity_classification (Sherlock Watsons)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_evaluate: evaluate submitted issue
    q_evaluate --> q_check_exclusion: check against invalid categories list
    q_check_exclusion --> q_excluded: matches exclusion (gas opt, wrong event, zero check, etc.)
    q_check_exclusion --> q_not_excluded: does not match exclusion
    q_excluded --> q_invalid: severity = Invalid
    q_invalid --> [*]: issue rejected
    q_not_excluded --> q_check_high: check High severity criteria
    q_check_high --> q_high_direct: direct loss of funds without extensive limitations
    q_check_high --> q_not_high: does not meet High criteria
    q_high_direct --> q_check_significant: loss >= 1% AND >= $10 of principal/yield/fees
    q_check_significant --> q_is_high: significant loss confirmed
    q_check_significant --> q_downgrade_to_med: loss not significant
    q_is_high --> q_check_frontrun_h: check if depends on front-running
    q_check_frontrun_h --> q_private_mempool_h: chain has private mempool
    q_check_frontrun_h --> q_high_confirmed: no front-running dependency or public mempool
    q_private_mempool_h --> q_downgrade_to_med: High downgraded to Medium
    q_high_confirmed --> [*]: severity = High
    q_not_high --> q_check_medium: check Medium severity criteria
    q_check_medium --> q_loss_constrained: loss of funds with external conditions or constraints
    q_check_medium --> q_core_break: breaks core contract functionality
    q_check_medium --> q_dos_check: denial of service evaluation
    q_check_medium --> q_invariant_break: breaks README-defined invariant
    q_check_medium --> q_not_medium: none apply
    q_loss_constrained --> q_check_relevant: loss >= 0.01% AND >= $10
    q_check_relevant --> q_med_candidate: relevant loss confirmed
    q_check_relevant --> q_not_medium: loss not relevant
    q_core_break --> q_med_candidate: core functionality broken
    q_invariant_break --> q_med_candidate: README invariant broken (if not conflicting common sense)
    q_dos_check --> q_dos_funds_locked: funds locked > 1 week
    q_dos_check --> q_dos_time_sensitive: impacts time-sensitive function
    q_dos_check --> q_dos_both: funds locked > 1 week AND time-sensitive impact
    q_dos_funds_locked --> q_med_candidate: Medium severity DoS
    q_dos_time_sensitive --> q_med_candidate: Medium severity DoS
    q_dos_both --> q_is_high: High severity DoS
    q_med_candidate --> q_check_frontrun_m: check if depends on front-running
    q_check_frontrun_m --> q_private_mempool_m: chain has private mempool
    q_check_frontrun_m --> q_medium_confirmed: no front-running dependency or public mempool
    q_private_mempool_m --> q_invalid: Medium downgraded to Invalid
    q_medium_confirmed --> [*]: severity = Medium
    q_not_medium --> q_invalid: severity = Invalid

    note right of q_check_high
        INV-001: High = direct fund loss without extensive external conditions
        INV-002: Significant loss = > 1% AND > $10 of principal/yield/fees
    end note

    note right of q_check_medium
        INV-003: Medium = fund loss with conditions, OR core functionality broken
        INV-004: Relevant loss = > 0.01% AND > $10
        INV-005: 0.01% loss replayable infinitely = treated as 100% loss
    end note

    note right of q_dos_check
        INV-006: DoS funds locked > 1 week = Medium
        INV-007: DoS time-sensitive function impacted = Medium
        INV-008: Both conditions = High
        INV-009: Single DoS < 1 week evaluated on single occurrence only
    end note
